+/**
+ * Mission item 5 (Oct 31) — word-level diff for the report-edit history.
+ *
+ * Renders like GitHub's word diff: unchanged words plain, removed words
+ * struck-through red, added words highlighted green — and it must work for
+ * RTL PERSIAN text, which rules out every naive line-diff (a reflowed
+ * paragraph would show as one giant replace). Words are the natural unit:
+ * the server's notes are free-text paragraphs and edits typically touch a
+ * few words.
+ *
+ * Algorithm: classic LCS over word tokens (word + its trailing whitespace,
+ * so spacing survives the roundtrip). Complexity O(n·m) — notes are capped
+ * at 5000 chars (~900 words) → ~810k cells, fine. A pathological guard
+ * falls back to whole-text del+add when either side exceeds the token cap
+ * (e.g. a future larger cap), so the dialog can never hang.
+ *
+ * This module is PURE (no React, no DB) so it is unit-testable from the
+ * audit suites via a plain node run.
+ */
+
